903:## Round 20 — one deadline at a time, criteria at the end, C17 alone (run 20261018-finish-everything)
904-
905-Found on 2026-10-17: `deadline end --session S` ended the newest open deadline, another run's; the criteria step
906-blocked at a stop while the task's own workflows still ran ("true | false at the end, never while the work runs");
907-the C17 tests fail whenever another session runs opencode.
908-
909-- **DL1 `--id D-xxxxxxxx`.** `deadline status | wait | end` with `--id` act on that deadline only, whatever its
910-  session or run. An id with no deadline file: `no deadline <id>` on stderr, exit 2. `status --id` of an ended
911-  deadline prints `<id> ended <time>` and exits 0.
912-- **DL2 `--run DIR`.** `deadline status | wait | end` with `--run` act on the newest open deadline whose `run` is DIR
913-  (compared as `deadline start --run` stores it, relative to the root). None: `no deadline for <DIR>`, exit 2.
914-- **DL3 `end` never guesses.** `deadline end` with neither `--id` nor `--run`, when more than one deadline is open in
915-  its scope (the `--session` given, or every session), ends none: it prints each open id with its run on stderr and
916-  exits 2. With exactly one open, it ends that one, as before.
917-- **DL4 Unchanged.** `status` and `wait` with neither flag keep today's choice (the session's newest running deadline).
918-
919-- **CR1 Criteria at the end.** At a `Stop`, while the session has an open deadline that is not up (DL4's choice for
920-  the session), the criteria step does not block, writes no failure and prints nothing (amended 03:12: a context line
921-  at `Stop` makes Claude Code continue the turn, so it woke a waiting agent at every stop). The step runs as before
922-  once that deadline is ended or up, or when the session has none. Every other step of the stop is unchanged.
923-
924-- **C17 alone.** The C17 tests put a `ps` first on `PATH` that prints the real `ps` output with every other process's
925-  `opencode run` line removed (the tests' own marked lines kept), so they pass while other sessions run opencode,
926-  and they no longer refuse to run then.
927-
928-- **XB1 crossed-build-check `timeout`.** `args.timeout` (seconds, a whole number from 60 to 3600, default 580) is the
929-  limit of every engine call and test command the workflow starts. Above 580 the step runs the command in the
930-  background and waits for it to end, since one Bash call is capped at 600 s. Anything else is `args.timeout must be a
931-  whole number of seconds from 60 to 3600`.
932-
933-Fails-if: `deadline end` with two open deadlines ends one without `--id` or `--run`; `--id` or `--run` acts on another
934-deadline; a stop inside an open, not-up deadline is blocked by the criteria step or writes a criteria failure; a stop
935-after the deadline ends skips the criteria step; a C17 test fails or refuses because another opencode runs; the
936-`timeout` given does not reach every engine call and test command.
937-
938:**Round 20, after its review (03:15, four findings, each reproduced by the reviewer).**
939-- **CR1a.** A deferred criteria step is no result at all: the stop goes on to its next step (the path ask) exactly as
940-  when the session touched no criteria file. Only the criteria step waits for the deadline.
941-- **DL5.** `deadline wait --mark` is a usage error (exit 2) with `--id` or `--run` too, before anything waits.
942-- **XB2.** Above 580 s a step starts each command as `( timeout <N> <command>; echo "exit $?" > <file>.exit ) &` and
943-  reads the exit from `<file>.exit` when it appears; a missing `.exit` file after the limit is a failed step, never a
944-  pass.
945-- **XB3.** Every test command the workflow starts (fail first, head) is run as `timeout <N> <test_cmd>`, as engine
946-  calls are; no prompt tells a step to use the Bash tool's 600000 ms limit for a command when N is below 580.
947-
948-Fails-if: a deferred criteria step stops the path ask; `wait --id … --mark` waits; a background step reports an exit
949-it could not read; a test command runs without `timeout <N>`.
950-
951:**Round 20, after the Codex review (09:00; findings 4 and 5 of `runs/20261018-finish-everything/nodes/codex-review.md`).**
952-- **XB4.** A test command is run as `timeout <N> bash -c '<test_cmd>'` (its single quotes written `'\''`), so the
953-  limit bounds the whole command, not only its first part; XB2's background form wraps the same.
954-- **C17b.** The C17 fake `ps` keeps a foreign `opencode run` line only when it holds the test's own marker; the CLI's
955-  own line and its parent's are kept by pid (the fake `ps` is a child of the CLI, so they are `$PPID` and that pid's
956-  parent), never by their text.
957-
958-Fails-if: a compound test command runs past `<N>`; a foreign `opencode run "second task"` line makes a C17 test fail.
